═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
CRITICAL: VALIDATION-ONLY PROMPT
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

YOU ARE NOT RESPONSIBLE FOR FIXING. Your job is to:
1. Accept the generated JSON plan
2. Run all 21 validation checks systematically
3. Report PASS or FAIL for each check
4. If ANY check fails: Output detailed error message with specifics
5. Do NOT attempt to regenerate or fix—let the generation phase handle that

This separation means you can FOCUS on systematic checking without worrying about creative solutions. Check exhaustively and report precisely.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
VALIDATION CHECKS REFERENCE (21 checks total)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

STRUCTURAL CHECKS (Format & Completeness): Checks 1-6
SEMANTIC CHECKS (Physical/Logical Validity): Checks 7-15
METADATA CHECKS (Plan Consistency): Checks 16-21

---

## CHECK 1: STAGE STRUCTURE (Format requirement)

RULE: Plan must use "stages" JSON object structure with numeric string keys ("1", "2", "3"), NOT a flat "subtasks" array.

DETECTION:
```javascript
if (plan.stages === undefined || typeof plan.stages !== 'object') {
  FAIL: "Plan missing 'stages' object. Found: " + Object.keys(plan)
}
if (Array.isArray(plan.stages)) {
  FAIL: "Plan uses 'stages' array instead of object. Must be: {'1': {...}, '2': {...}}"
}
if (plan.subtasks && typeof plan.subtasks === 'array') {
  FAIL: "Plan uses 'subtasks' array. Rename to 'stages' object with numeric keys"
}
```

PASS CONDITION: plan.stages exists AND is object (not array)

ERROR MESSAGE FORMAT:
```
✗ CHECK 1 FAILED: Stage Structure
  Plan must use 'stages' object. Current structure: [TYPE]
  Example of valid format:
  {
    "stages": {
      "1": { "Worker1": {...}, "Worker2": {...} },
      "2": { "Worker1": {...}, "Worker2": {...} }
    }
  }
```

---

## CHECK 2: STAGE COMPLETENESS (All workers in every stage)

RULE: Every stage must have entries for all workers. Each worker either has:
  - A task with coordinates and prompt, OR
  - Explicit status "rest" if idle

DETECTION:
```javascript
const stageKeys = Object.keys(plan.stages).map(k => parseInt(k)).sort();
const expectedWorkerCount = plan.workerCount || 2;

for (let stageNum of stageKeys) {
  const stage = plan.stages[stageNum.toString()];
  const workersInStage = Object.keys(stage).filter(k => k.startsWith('Worker'));

  if (workersInStage.length !== expectedWorkerCount) {
    FAIL: `Stage ${stageNum} has ${workersInStage.length} workers, expected ${expectedWorkerCount}`
  }

  // Check each worker has task or rest
  for (let workerName of ['Worker1', 'Worker2', ...]) {
    if (!stage[workerName]) {
      FAIL: `Stage ${stageNum} missing ${workerName}`
    }
    if (!stage[workerName].subtask && !stage[workerName].status) {
      FAIL: `Stage ${stageNum} ${workerName} has no task or status`
    }
  }
}
```

PASS CONDITION: Every stage has all expected workers with either task or status

ERROR MESSAGE FORMAT:
```
✗ CHECK 2 FAILED: Stage Completeness
  Stage [N] is missing Worker[X]. All stages must include all workers.
  Found workers in Stage N: [LIST]
  Expected workers: [LIST]
  Add missing worker with either:
    - "task": "...", "coordinates": {...}
    - "status": "rest"
```

---

## CHECK 3: STAGE ORDERING (Sequential, no gaps)

RULE: Stages must be numbered 1, 2, 3, 4, ... with no gaps, duplicates, or out-of-order

DETECTION:
```javascript
const stageNumbers = Object.keys(plan.stages)
  .map(k => parseInt(k))
  .sort((a, b) => a - b);

const expectedSequence = Array.from({length: Math.max(...stageNumbers)}, (_, i) => i + 1);

if (JSON.stringify(stageNumbers) !== JSON.stringify(expectedSequence)) {
  FAIL: `Stages not sequential. Found: [${stageNumbers}], Expected: [${expectedSequence}]`
}
```

PASS CONDITION: Stage keys form continuous sequence [1, 2, 3, ..., N]

ERROR MESSAGE FORMAT:
```
✗ CHECK 3 FAILED: Stage Ordering
  Stages not in order.
  Found: [1, 2, 4, 5]  (gap at 3)
  Expected: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
  Renumber stages sequentially with no gaps.
```

---

## CHECK 4: STAGE COUNT BALANCE (Workers carry similar load)

RULE: Number of stages for Worker1 and Worker2 should differ by at most 1

DETECTION:
```javascript
const worker1Stages = Object.values(plan.stages)
  .filter(stage => stage.Worker1 && stage.Worker1.subtask && stage.Worker1.subtask !== 'rest')
  .length;

const worker2Stages = Object.values(plan.stages)
  .filter(stage => stage.Worker2 && stage.Worker2.subtask && stage.Worker2.subtask !== 'rest')
  .length;

const difference = Math.abs(worker1Stages - worker2Stages);

if (difference > 1) {
  FAIL: `Stage imbalance: Worker1=[${worker1Stages}], Worker2=[${worker2Stages}], diff=${difference} > 1`
}
```

PASS CONDITION: |Worker1_stageCount - Worker2_stageCount| ≤ 1

ERROR MESSAGE FORMAT:
```
✗ CHECK 4 FAILED: Stage Count Balance
  Worker1 has [A] stages with tasks
  Worker2 has [B] stages with tasks
  Difference: |A - B| = [DIFF] (max allowed: 1)
  Redistribute so both have approximately equal work.
```

---

## CHECK 5: COORDINATES DEFINED (All X,Y,Z specified)

RULE: Every task must specify explicit coordinate boundaries: xMin, xMax, yMin, yMax, zMin, zMax

DETECTION:
```javascript
const requiredCoords = ['xMin', 'xMax', 'yMin', 'yMax', 'zMin', 'zMax'];

for (let stage of Object.values(plan.stages)) {
  for (let worker of Object.values(stage)) {
    if (!worker.coordinates) {
      FAIL: `${worker.worker} in stage ${worker.stageNumber} missing coordinates object`
    }

    for (let coord of requiredCoords) {
      if (worker.coordinates[coord] === undefined) {
        FAIL: `${worker.worker} stage ${worker.stageNumber} missing ${coord}`
      }
      if (typeof worker.coordinates[coord] !== 'number') {
        FAIL: `${worker.worker} stage ${worker.stageNumber} ${coord} not a number: ${worker.coordinates[coord]}`
      }
    }
  }
}
```

PASS CONDITION: All tasks have xMin, xMax, yMin, yMax, zMin, zMax as numbers

ERROR MESSAGE FORMAT:
```
✗ CHECK 5 FAILED: Coordinates Defined
  Stage [N] Worker[X] missing coordinate: [COORD]
  Must specify: xMin, xMax, yMin, yMax, zMin, zMax (all numbers)
  Example:
    "coordinates": {
      "xMin": 298,
      "xMax": 303,
      "yMin": -60,
      "yMax": -59,
      "zMin": -528,
      "zMax": -525
    }
```

---

## CHECK 6: CONSTRAINTS PRESENT (3+ per task)

RULE: Every task must have at least 3 "Do NOT" constraints

DETECTION:
```javascript
for (let stage of Object.values(plan.stages)) {
  for (let worker of Object.values(stage)) {
    if (!worker.constraints || !Array.isArray(worker.constraints)) {
      FAIL: `${worker.worker} stage ${worker.stageNumber} has no constraints array`
    }
    if (worker.constraints.length < 3) {
      FAIL: `${worker.worker} stage ${worker.stageNumber} has only ${worker.constraints.length} constraints (need 3+)`
    }
  }
}
```

PASS CONDITION: All tasks have constraints array with length ≥ 3

ERROR MESSAGE FORMAT:
```
✗ CHECK 6 FAILED: Constraints Present
  Stage [N] Worker[X] has only [K] constraints (need 3+)
  Current: [LIST]
  Add at least [3-K] more constraints covering:
    - Coordinate boundaries (do NOT place beyond...)
    - What NOT to break
    - What NOT to overlap
    - Assumptions about other workers
```

