## CHECK 7: Y-LEVEL PROGRESSION (Different levels per stage type)

RULE: Foundation, Walls, Roof must each have DIFFERENT Y-ranges

DETECTION:
```javascript
// Extract all stage Y-ranges
const stageYRanges = {};
for (let stageNum of Object.keys(plan.stages).map(k => parseInt(k))) {
  const stage = plan.stages[stageNum.toString()];
  const worker1 = stage.Worker1;

  if (worker1 && worker1.coordinates) {
    stageYRanges[stageNum] = {
      yMin: worker1.coordinates.yMin,
      yMax: worker1.coordinates.yMax,
      range: worker1.coordinates.yMax - worker1.coordinates.yMin
    };
  }
}

// Check that consecutive stages don't have same Y-range
const stageNums = Object.keys(stageYRanges).map(k => parseInt(k)).sort();
for (let i = 0; i < stageNums.length - 1; i++) {
  const stage1 = stageYRanges[stageNums[i]];
  const stage2 = stageYRanges[stageNums[i + 1]];

  if (stage1.yMin === stage2.yMin || stage1.yMax === stage2.yMax) {
    FAIL: `Stage ${stageNums[i]} and ${stageNums[i+1]} both at y:${stage1.yMin}-${stage1.yMax} (same Y-level)`
  }
}
```

PASS CONDITION: Consecutive stages use different Y ranges

ERROR MESSAGE FORMAT:
```
✗ CHECK 7 FAILED: Y-Level Progression
  Stages [N] and [N+1] both at same Y level:
  Stage [N]: y:[A] to [B]
  Stage [N+1]: y:[A] to [B]
  Foundation, walls, roof must be at different Y levels.
  Fix: Adjust Stage [N+1] to higher Y range: y:[C] to [D]
```

