## CHECK 8: NO Y-LEVEL OVERLAP IN CONSECUTIVE STAGES

RULE: For each worker, consecutive stages must NOT overlap in Y coordinates

DETECTION:
```javascript
// For each worker, check Y-overlap between consecutive stages
for (let worker of ['Worker1', 'Worker2']) {
  const workerStages = [];

  for (let stageNum of Object.keys(plan.stages).map(k => parseInt(k)).sort()) {
    const stage = plan.stages[stageNum.toString()];
    if (stage[worker] && stage[worker].coordinates) {
      workerStages.push({
        stageNum: stageNum,
        yMin: stage[worker].coordinates.yMin,
        yMax: stage[worker].coordinates.yMax
      });
    }
  }

  // Check consecutive pairs
  for (let i = 0; i < workerStages.length - 1; i++) {
    const s1 = workerStages[i];
    const s2 = workerStages[i + 1];

    // Check if they overlap: s1.yMax >= s2.yMin (they overlap)
    if (s1.yMax >= s2.yMin) {
      FAIL: `${worker} Stage ${s1.stageNum}→${s2.stageNum} Y-overlap: ${s1.stageNum} yMax=${s1.yMax}, ${s2.stageNum} yMin=${s2.yMin}`
    }
  }
}
```

PASS CONDITION: For each worker, stage[N].yMax < stage[N+1].yMin (strict <, not ≤)

ERROR MESSAGE FORMAT:
```
✗ CHECK 8 FAILED: Y-Level Overlap
  Worker[X] Stage [N→N+1] Y-overlap:
  Stage [N]: yMin=[A], yMax=[B]
  Stage [N+1]: yMin=[C], yMax=[D]
  They overlap at y=[RANGE] (yMax[N]=[B] is >= yMin[N+1]=[C])
  Fix: Shift Stage [N+1] higher or lower to eliminate overlap.
  Example: Stage [N] y:-59 to -57, Stage [N+1] y:-56 to -54 (no overlap)
```

