## CHECK 10: NO WITHIN-STAGE DEPENDENCIES (All stages parallelizable)

RULE: Within any single stage, neither worker should depend on the other

DETECTION:
```javascript
const dependencyKeywords = [
  'wait for', 'after', 'once', 'when', 'until', 'depend',
  'complete', 'finish', 'support', 'on top of', 'above'
];

for (let stage of Object.values(plan.stages)) {
  const w1 = stage.Worker1;
  const w2 = stage.Worker2;

  if (w1 && w2) {
    const w1Text = (w1.subtask || '').toLowerCase();
    const w2Text = (w2.subtask || '').toLowerCase();

    // Check if W1 mentions W2 or has dependency language
    for (let keyword of dependencyKeywords) {
      if (w1Text.includes(keyword) && 
          (w1Text.includes('worker2') || w1Text.includes('second worker'))) {
        FAIL: `Stage ${w1.stageNumber} W1 depends on W2: "${w1.subtask}"`
      }
    }

    // Same for W2 depending on W1
    for (let keyword of dependencyKeywords) {
      if (w2Text.includes(keyword) && 
          (w2Text.includes('worker1') || w2Text.includes('first worker'))) {
        FAIL: `Stage ${w2.stageNumber} W2 depends on W1: "${w2.subtask}"`
      }
    }
  }
}
```

PASS CONDITION: No task explicitly depends on other worker completing first

ERROR MESSAGE FORMAT:
```
✗ CHECK 10 FAILED: Within-Stage Dependencies
  Stage [N] has sequential dependency:
  Worker1: "[Task A]"
  Worker2: "[Task B - depends on A]"
  Both workers must be able to work simultaneously.
  Fix: Split into separate stages or remove dependency language.
```

