## CHECK 11: ROOF RIDGE ACCESSIBLE (At least one worker can reach it)

RULE: roofRidgeX must be within or adjacent to at least one worker's scope

DETECTION:
```javascript
const ridgeX = plan.metadata?.roofRidgeX;
const w1XMin = plan.metadata?.worker1XRange?.[0];
const w1XMax = plan.metadata?.worker1XRange?.[1];
const w2XMin = plan.metadata?.worker2XRange?.[0];
const w2XMax = plan.metadata?.worker2XRange?.[1];

if (ridgeX !== undefined) {
  const inW1 = (ridgeX >= w1XMin && ridgeX <= w1XMax);
  const inW2 = (ridgeX >= w2XMin && ridgeX <= w2XMax);
  const atBoundary = (ridgeX === w1XMax || ridgeX === w2XMin);

  if (!inW1 && !inW2 && !atBoundary) {
    FAIL: `Roof ridge unreachable: ridgeX=${ridgeX}, W1 scope=[${w1XMin},${w1XMax}], W2 scope=[${w2XMin},${w2XMax}]`
  }
}
```

PASS CONDITION: roofRidgeX is in [W1_xMin, W1_xMax] OR [W2_xMin, W2_xMax] OR at boundary

ERROR MESSAGE FORMAT:
```
✗ CHECK 11 FAILED: Roof Ridge Accessibility
  Roof ridge at X=[RIDGE]
  Worker1 scope: X=[W1_MIN]-[W1_MAX]
  Worker2 scope: X=[W2_MIN]-[W2_MAX]
  Ridge X=[RIDGE] is outside all worker scopes!
  Fix: Move ridge to X=[VALUE in range] or extend worker scope.
```

