## CHECK 14: NO DUPLICATE ELEMENT ASSIGNMENTS

RULE: Foundation, walls, etc. assigned to exactly ONE worker per stage (or both with spatial division)

DETECTION:
```javascript
const elementTypes = ['foundation', 'floor', 'walls', 'roof', 'interior'];

for (let stage of Object.values(plan.stages)) {
  const w1Task = (stage.Worker1?.subtask || '').toLowerCase();
  const w2Task = (stage.Worker2?.subtask || '').toLowerCase();

  for (let element of elementTypes) {
    const w1Has = w1Task.includes(element);
    const w2Has = w2Task.includes(element);

    if (w1Has && w2Has) {
      // Both mention same element - check if spatial division exists
      const hasSpatialMarkers = 
        (w1Task.includes('west') || w1Task.includes('north') || w1Task.includes('left')) &&
        (w2Task.includes('east') || w2Task.includes('south') || w2Task.includes('right'));

      if (!hasSpatialMarkers) {
        FAIL: `Stage ${stage.Worker1?.stageNumber} both workers assign to '${element}' without spatial division`
      }
    }
  }
}
```

PASS CONDITION: If both workers build same element, they have clear spatial division (west/east, etc.)

ERROR MESSAGE FORMAT:
